{#- luria/view_templates/journal-book.md.j2

One book of a journal (ADR-020), as a template luria ships (ADR-147).
The context is built by `journal.book_context`:

  generated_from  the journal's directory, relative to the root
  title, label    the journal's title and this book's period
  count           how many entries the book holds
  entries         oldest first; each has anchor (the timestamp id), slug
                  (the heading's own anchor, which the contents list links),
                  stamp (short, for the contents), created (full), title,
                  tags and body

`heading` and `section` live in `journal-book-parts.md.j2` because
`journal.entry_anchors` renders them too: a heading's slug depends on every
heading before it, the bodies' own included, so the slugs are computed from
the same markup rather than from a second copy of it.
-#}
